b923398c-2cbf-453b-adab-408c2409739d	01920000-1000-7000-8000-000000000001	2025-09-11 22:21:22.123	2025-09-11 22:21:22.123	Wide Corp Mission & Values	# Wide Corp Solutions - Our Foundation\n\n## Mission Statement\nWide Corp Solutions exists to empower businesses through innovative technology solutions that drive growth, efficiency, and competitive advantage.\n\n## Core Values\n- **Excellence**: We deliver exceptional quality in everything we do\n- **Innovation**: We embrace cutting-edge technologies and creative problem-solving\n- **Integrity**: We build trust through honest, transparent business practices\n- **Collaboration**: We believe in the power of teamwork and partnership\n- **Growth**: We are committed to continuous learning and improvement\n\n## Cultural Foundation\nWe foster an environment where creativity thrives, diverse perspectives are valued, and every team member is empowered to contribute to our shared success.	published	lore	world	01920000-1000-7000-8000-000000000001	95	Define Wide Corp's core mission, values, and cultural identity	{}	policy	lore
9cad6d7e-5e8e-4530-aecd-60475db64706	01920000-1000-7000-8000-000000000001	2025-09-11 22:21:35.852	2025-09-11 22:21:35.852	Wide Corp Operating Procedures	# Wide Corp Solutions - Standard Operating Procedures\n\n## Decision Making Framework\n1. **Data-Driven Decisions**: All major decisions must be supported by quantitative analysis\n2. **Stakeholder Consultation**: Key stakeholders must be consulted before implementation\n3. **Risk Assessment**: Potential risks and mitigation strategies must be documented\n\n## Project Delivery Standards\n1. **Client Communication**: Weekly status updates required for all active projects\n2. **Quality Gates**: Code review and testing required before any production deployment\n3. **Documentation**: All deliverables must include comprehensive documentation\n\n## Team Collaboration Rules\n1. **Daily Standups**: 15-minute team sync every morning at 9:00 AM EST\n2. **Sprint Planning**: Bi-weekly planning sessions with full team participation\n3. **Retrospectives**: Monthly process improvement reviews\n\n## Performance Standards\n- Client satisfaction rating: Minimum 4.5/5.0\n- Project delivery: On-time delivery rate of 95%+\n- Code quality: Zero critical security vulnerabilities\n- Response time: Client inquiries answered within 4 business hours	published	canon	world	01920000-1000-7000-8000-000000000001	88	Document our standard operating procedures and performance standards	{}	procedure	canon
a53b72a9-0b60-477e-abbe-dd3fc83cd44c	01920000-1000-7000-8000-000000000001	2025-09-11 22:26:16.766	2025-09-11 22:26:16.766	API Infrastructure Vision & Goals	# API Infrastructure Project - Vision & Goals\n\n## Project Vision\nTo build a world-class, scalable API infrastructure that serves as the backbone for all Wide Corp digital products and services. Our API will be the foundation that enables rapid innovation, seamless integrations, and exceptional developer experiences.\n\n## Success Definition\n- **Performance**: Sub-100ms average response times across all endpoints\n- **Reliability**: 99.9% uptime with automatic failover capabilities\n- **Developer Experience**: Comprehensive documentation and SDKs that developers love\n- **Scalability**: Handle 10x current traffic without architecture changes\n- **Security**: Zero-trust architecture with comprehensive audit trails\n\n## Strategic Impact\n- Enable faster time-to-market for new features and products\n- Reduce integration complexity for partners and clients\n- Create new revenue streams through API monetization\n- Establish Wide Corp as a technology leader in our industry\n\n## Team Motivation\nThis project represents our opportunity to build something that will power Wide Corp's growth for years to come. Every endpoint we design and every optimization we make directly impacts our ability to serve our clients better.	published	lore	project	01920000-1003-7003-8003-000000000021	92	Define the vision and success criteria for our API infrastructure project	{}	internal	lore
9dd4d002-2270-4477-976c-fae51c83ff67	01920000-1000-7000-8000-000000000001	2025-09-11 22:26:36.887	2025-09-11 22:26:36.887	API Infrastructure Technical Requirements	# API Infrastructure - Technical Requirements & Constraints\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n### Performance\n- Response time: < 100ms for 95th percentile\n- Throughput: Minimum 10,000 requests/second per service\n- Database queries: < 50ms average execution time\n- Memory usage: < 512MB per service instance\n\n### Reliability & Availability\n- Uptime: 99.9% (max 8.77 hours downtime/year)\n- Automatic failover: < 30 seconds recovery time\n- Circuit breaker patterns for all external dependencies\n- Graceful degradation for non-critical features\n\n### Security Requirements\n- OAuth 2.0 + PKCE for authentication\n- Rate limiting: 1000 requests/hour per API key\n- All data encrypted at rest (AES-256)\n- TLS 1.3 minimum for all communications\n- Security headers: OWASP compliance mandatory\n\n## Technical Constraints\n\n### Technology Stack\n- Runtime: Node.js 20+ or Go 1.21+\n- Database: PostgreSQL 15+ with connection pooling\n- Cache: Redis 7+ for session and response caching\n- Message Queue: RabbitMQ or AWS SQS for async processing\n\n### Architecture Requirements\n- Microservices architecture with clear service boundaries\n- Event-driven communication between services\n- OpenAPI 3.0 specification for all endpoints\n- Containerized deployment (Docker + Kubernetes)\n- Blue-green deployment strategy required\n\n### Quality Gates\n- Code coverage: Minimum 80% for all services\n- Static analysis: Zero critical security vulnerabilities\n- Load testing: Must pass 2x expected peak load\n- Documentation: Complete API docs with examples\n- Monitoring: Full observability with metrics, logs, and traces	published	canon	project	01920000-1003-7003-8003-000000000021	89	Document technical requirements and quality gates for API infrastructure	{}	procedure	canon
8e1f47ba-d72c-42c8-9564-babc36179c4b	01920000-1000-7000-8000-000000000001	2025-09-11 22:26:58.592	2025-09-11 22:26:58.592	AI Integration Initiative - Transforming Our Future	# AI Integration Initiative - Transforming Our Future\n\n## Vision Statement\nTo position Wide Corp as an AI-first organization that leverages artificial intelligence not just as a feature, but as a fundamental capability that transforms how we solve problems, serve customers, and create value.\n\n## Why This Matters\nAI represents the biggest technological shift since the internet. Organizations that successfully integrate AI will have insurmountable competitive advantages:\n- **10x faster problem-solving** through intelligent automation\n- **Personalized experiences** that anticipate customer needs\n- **Data-driven insights** that reveal hidden opportunities\n- **Operational efficiency** that scales without proportional cost increases\n\n## Success Vision\n- Every Wide Corp product includes intelligent features that customers love\n- Our team uses AI tools daily to enhance productivity and creativity\n- We've reduced manual, repetitive work by 70% through intelligent automation\n- Our AI capabilities become a key differentiator in client pitches\n- We attract top talent who want to work with cutting-edge AI technology\n\n## Cultural Impact\nThis project isn't just about technology—it's about evolving our culture:\n- **Curiosity over Routine**: Encouraging experimentation with AI tools\n- **Augmented Intelligence**: AI enhances human creativity rather than replacing it\n- **Ethical Leadership**: Setting industry standards for responsible AI use\n- **Continuous Learning**: Building an organization that adapts as AI evolves\n\n## Legacy Goal\nIn 5 years, when people think of innovative AI applications in our industry, they think of Wide Corp first.	published	lore	project	01920000-1003-7003-8003-000000000036	94	Articulate the transformative vision and cultural impact of our AI initiative	{}	internal	lore
37752400-254b-4ed2-a26e-0554a632f0cb	01920000-1000-7000-8000-000000000001	2025-09-11 23:32:06.206	2025-09-11 23:32:06.207	Wide Corp Mission Statement	# Wide Corp Solutions Mission\n\n## Our Purpose\nWide Corp Solutions exists to deliver innovative technology solutions that transform businesses and empower growth. We bridge the gap between complex technical challenges and practical business outcomes.\n\n## Our Values\n- **Innovation First**: We embrace cutting-edge technology to solve real-world problems\n- **Client Success**: Our clients success is our success - we measure ourselves by their achievements\n- **Technical Excellence**: We maintain the highest standards in code quality, architecture, and delivery\n- **Continuous Learning**: We invest in our teams growth and stay ahead of industry trends\n- **Collaborative Partnership**: We work as an extension of our clients teams, not just a vendor\n\n## Our Vision\nTo be the trusted technology partner that enables businesses to achieve breakthrough results through digital transformation.	published	lore	world	01920000-1000-7000-8000-000000000001	95	\N	{}	internal	general
29d21bb6-a278-42b2-903f-50acbdc02388	01920000-1000-7000-8000-000000000001	2025-09-11 23:32:22.458	2025-09-11 23:32:22.458	Wide Corp Development Standards	# Wide Corp Development Standards & Canon\n\n## Code Quality Standards\n\n### 1. Code Review Process\n- **All code must be peer-reviewed** before merging to main branch\n- **Minimum 2 approvals required** for production deployments\n- **No exceptions** - even hotfixes require review\n\n### 2. Testing Requirements\n- **Unit test coverage minimum: 80%**\n- **Integration tests required** for all API endpoints\n- **E2E tests required** for critical user journeys\n- **All tests must pass** before deployment\n\n### 3. Documentation Standards\n- **README.md required** for all repositories\n- **API documentation** must be auto-generated and current\n- **Architecture decisions** documented in ADRs\n- **Code comments** for business logic and complex algorithms\n\n### 4. Security Requirements\n- **No hardcoded secrets** - all configuration via environment variables\n- **Input validation required** on all user inputs\n- **Authentication required** on all non-public endpoints\n- **Regular security audits** of dependencies\n\n### 5. Performance Standards\n- **API response time** under 200ms for 95th percentile\n- **Page load time** under 2 seconds\n- **Database queries optimized** - no N+1 problems\n- **Caching strategy** for frequently accessed data\n\n## Non-Negotiable Rules\n\n1. **No direct commits to main** - all changes via pull requests\n2. **Production deployments only during business hours** (9 AM - 5 PM EST)\n3. **Rollback plan required** for all production changes\n4. **Client data encryption** at rest and in transit\n5. **Regular backups** - tested monthly	published	canon	world	01920000-1000-7000-8000-000000000001	90	\N	{}	internal	general
